{"duration_api_ms":496453,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"7883e351-c8fd-4787-84c4-dc20b51c9ad1","total_cost_usd":6.409563,"usage":{"input_tokens":130,"cache_creation_input_tokens":170184,"cache_read_input_tokens":7659034,"output_tokens":34840,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":12234},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":170184,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1141,"cache_read_input_tokens":179936,"cache_creation_input_tokens":253,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":253},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":6451,"outputTokens":21,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.006556,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":130,"outputTokens":34840,"cacheReadInputTokens":7659034,"cacheCreationInputTokens":170184,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":6.403007000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":12234,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":65,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Verdict: changes requested → `to-dev`.** One blocking finding, and it's not in the code.\n\n## The code is good, and I attacked it rather than read it\n\nSeven **narrowing** mutants (never delete-only), each grep-confirmed present before measuring, each applied to an isolated `git archive HEAD` copy so the worktree was never touched — **7/7 killed** at both `VerifyRepository` and `VerifyAssignedSections`, plus the `main -> run -> VerifyAssignedSections` chain. The load-bearing one (`!= coverageFull` → `== coverageSliver`) restores rev1's behaviour — `-section 9.2` exits 0 on a 0/35 binding — and reddens four tests.\n\nAlso verified: rev1's blocking finding is genuinely closed (15.2 / 7.3 / 13.14.5 all exit 1 at unmeasured 0/0 with mandatory gaps); the three named slivers are re-declared, not re-bound; anti-vacuity holds both ways; coverage is a real measured ratio (`2/394` over 48 bindings, pinned byte-exact); no assertion weakened. I also probed the disclosed residual directly — enumerated all three §6.5 clauses against one existing acceptance case, declared `full`, re-pinned the digest → admitted. That is *exactly and only* the class README declares out of scope, and it's review-gated twice over. No wider hole.\n\nFull repo validation re-run on the candidate tree, all exit 0, coverage matching the producer's claim (specdoc 100.0%, traceability 86.4%, tracecheck 88.5%).\n\n## What blocks it\n\n`BUG-260902-2m7slg_coverage-gate.md` — the artifact DoD item 2 names — was never updated after the rev1 rework. No superseded marker, reads as current, and its **Scope: what the gate can and cannot decide** section restates the model the rev1 review rejected and rev2 removed:\n\n| Artifact says | Shipped binary does |\n| --- | --- |\n| level `declarative`, \"carries no obligation of its own\" | level `unmeasured`; that claim being false is the whole rev2 fix |\n| admission requires `full` **or** `declarative` | requires `full`, nothing else |\n| \"four sections … admitted with no clause evidence\" | three `unmeasured` bindings, all refused |\n| admission succeeds for 6.2, 13.14.5, 7.3, 15.2 | 6.2 → exit 0; other three → exit **1** |\n| `-section 6.2 -section 13.14.5` → exit 0 | exit **1** |\n| fenced \"tracecheck output\": `declarative=3` | command emits `unmeasured=3`; no build prints that token |\n\nTwo of those are presented as measured exit codes and verbatim command output, and they aren't. A reader taking the primary artifact at face value concludes §15.2, §7.3 and §13.14.5 are owned scopes — the precise \"already owned, so I can legitimately do nothing\" state this Bug exists to destroy. rev1 shipped that belief in code; rev2 fixed the code and left it standing in the artifact.\n\n**Fix:** `task-board resource update` that one artifact in place, reproducing the report line from the real command. No `internal/` change requested.\n\nAttached: `_review-verdict.md`, `_review-mutation-log.md`, `_review-artifact-claims-recheck.log`.","ttft_ms":1931,"type":"result","duration_ms":787159,"uuid":"dc41ce9e-6471-4384-b6fc-f64f261a2a42","ttft_stream_ms":1234,"time_to_request_ms":16,"queued_turn_count":0}
